WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.600
Heads up, major Avengers: Infinity War spoilers
coming your way.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.560
On top of having the most devastating ending
the Marvel Cinematic Universe has ever seen,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.860
Infinity War has a pretty bleak beginning
and middle as well, full of goodbyes to favorite

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.780
characters right from the opening scene.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.800
While audiences wait to see who returns to
finish the fight in Avengers 4, one performer

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.540
in the long-running series has just let people
know he's probably not coming back.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.800
Idris Elba, the English actor who played the
Asgardian guardian Heimdall, bid a fond farewell

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.080
to his character on Twitter.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.180
In the post, he wrote "#SpoilerAlert Gonna
miss my guy…Heimdall…"

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.280
The post seemingly confirmed that the keeper
of the Bifrost , who was among the very first

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:42.290
characters to meet their demise during Thanos'
assault, was one of the Marvel heroes we could

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.790
consider gone for good.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.940
"I hope they remember you."

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.260
But regardless of what Elba says now, the
record seems to show that he's had anything

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.260
but a loving public relationship with Marvel
Studios.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.780
As far back as Thor: The Dark World, Elba
was making delightfully unfriendly comments

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.060
to the media about how Marvel movies are,
quote, "torture", and how the indignity of

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.400
working on them, quote, "ripped [his] heart
out".

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:05.980
"Sorry about that."

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.900
Of course, with the central MacGuffin of Infinity
War being a magic glove that can turn back

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:16.060
time, there's no telling whether or not Elba
is truly going to be free from the franchise.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.860
After all, Avengers 4 wrapped filming in January,
before Infinity War was even released.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.439
Elba may have Heimdall in the rear view, but
that doesn't mean his character doesn't have

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:26.200
a scene or two in the fourth movie.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.330
If the actor's Instagram is anything to go
by, Elba spent Infinity War weekend racing

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.940
single-seater Formula E cars in Paris, France.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.240
Doesn't seem like he's too bummed about his
newfound freedom.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:40.400
But if he does end up making a surprise return,
well,he wouldn't be the first Asgardian warrior

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.380
to come back to life.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.200
Avengers: Infinity War continues to set box
office records, and the next movie in the

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.460
MCU series, Ant-Man and the Wasp, is set to
swarm theaters in early July.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:51.640
Thanks for watching!

